2.3 Uses/functions (WHY)
\par
As mentioned above, different types of information feed into FM systems at different times.
\par
A variety of information is gathered to serve the multiple needs of FM. Information from the
\par
early stages of a facility up to the construction phase is used to learn about the building and
\par
its nature, spatial plan, etc. On the other hand, business operations related information such
\par
as occupancy rate, business functional needs and market information are gathered to
\par
perform daily FM activities to support the current business and secure the future potential
\par
business opportunities. This information assists to maintain a flexible built environment,
\par
capable of adapting to changing business needs. Moreover, operational and maintenance
\par
information are used to upkeep a sustainable built environment.ECAM
\par
