\par
Of the 14 potential competing treatment sequences,
\par
sequences 7 and 11, which included vedolizumab and tofac-
\par
itinib, were the more effective alternatives in anti-TNF{$\alpha$} naive
\par
patients with active moderate-to-severe UC. When costs were
\par
considered, sequences 7 (vedolizumab used as the first t-line
\par
treatment and tofacitinib used as the second -line treatment) and
\par
11 (tofacitinib used as the firstt-line treatment and vedolizumab
\par
used as the second -line treatment) yielded an ICER value of
\par
\pounds 27,723/QALY (sequence 7) and 26,574/QALY (sequence 11) in
