3. Methodology
\par
3.1 Data collection
\par
The context of the data that were collected for this study was WeChat, which was chosen
\par
primarily because it is the most popular social network application in China. WeChat was
\par
chosen to collect data for several reasons. First, it is a very popular social network application
\par
with more than 60m members as of May 2016 (www.analysys.cn). Second, a social
\par
recommender system called``Gouwuquan'' is embedded in WeChat. It provides a platform for
\par
WeChat members to share their past online purchase experience with pictures and words.
\par
Other members can add comments and browse the profiles of the recommendation
\par
contributors. Profile page of members contains all of their recommendations, activities on the
\par
platform, and other members' comments and likes of the contributor. Furthermore, other
\par
members can buy recommended products by clicking a hyperlink to an online shop. We think
\par
that investigating the social recommender system in WeChat can help to us better understand
\par
the impact of social recommendations on customer decisions.OIR
