\par
Appendix. Construct items
\par
Recommendation persuasiveness
\par
{$\bullet$} RP 1: the recommendation arguments are convincing.
\par
{$\bullet$} RP 2: the recommendation arguments are strong.
\par
{$\bullet$} RP 3: the recommendation arguments persuasive.
\par
{$\bullet$} RP 4: the recommendation arguments are good.
\par
Recommendation completeness
\par
{$\bullet$} RC 1: the recommendation provides a complete description.
\par
{$\bullet$} RC 2: the recommendation covers all of the necessary topics.
\par
{$\bullet$} RC 3: the recommendation provides sufficient information.
\par
{$\bullet$} RC 4: the recommendation provides relatively comprehensive information.
\par
Trust in recommendations
\par
{$\bullet$} TR 1: I think the recommendation is credible.
\par
{$\bullet$} TR 2: I trust the recommendation.
\par
{$\bullet$} TR 3: I believe the recommendation is trustworthy.
\par
Perceived value
\par
{$\bullet$} PV 1: the social recommender system makes my shopping easier.
\par
{$\bullet$} PV 2: the social recommender system saves me time.
\par
{$\bullet$} PV 3: the social recommender system is useful for my shopping.
\par
Purchase intention
\par
{$\bullet$} PI 1: I would consider buying the recommended products.
\par
{$\bullet$} PI 2: I am likely to buy the recommended products.
\par
{$\bullet$} PI 3: I am willing to buy the recommended products.
