\par
tions by approximating continuous chance and utility nodes
\par
to mixtures of truncated exponential functions and mixtures
\par
of polynomials. However, these methods are not closed for
\par
non-linear deterministic functions and their computation can-
\par
not currently be fully-automated. MCMC methods have also
\par
been used to compute HIDs [41], [42] but their limitations
\par
are similar to the Markov chain VOI methods discussed in
