C. SUMMARY OF THE RESULTS
\par
Both the DD and DD-Fixed approaches accurately calcu-
\par
late the EVPPI values even with high convergence threshold
\par
settings. Starting from the convergence threshold of 10-2
\par
,
\par
the results of DD are close to the results of the NTL approach
\par
with 10,000 \texttimes 1000 inner and outer level samples, which we
\par
assume to be the ``true'' result. The results of both DD-Fixed
\par
and DD converge to the true values starting from the 10-3
\par
threshold setting. This also illustrates that DD successfully
\par
calculates the posteriors of the utility variables that are com-
\par
posed of mixture distributions with constants.
\par
Computation speed was the main limitation of our method.
\par
Although both DD and DD-Fixed were generally faster
\par
than NTL, they were slower than the sampling-based
\par
approaches at all convergence threshold settings with accept-
\par
able accuracy.
\par
