As most of the previous literature focused on supplier selection of manufacturing companies, but
\par
less on retail companies, we were inspired to develop a general measure for SSS and explore a feasible
\par
evaluation method. The integrated method of DEMATEL-ANP-VIKOR with hybrid information
\par
aggregation is finally proposed to help FX Supermarket select the suitable sustainable supplier from
\par
the above four alternative suppliers.
\par
4.2. Data Collection
\par
The data were collected within three phases. The first phase of our research investigates the
\par
interrelations of the dimension and criteria according to performance measure for sustainable suppliers
\par
from May to June 2017. In this stage, we originally issued 15 invitations to experts in the industry, 40
\par
invitations to retail companies, and 5 to research institutions. Finally, a total of 20 experts, including 5
\par
from industry associations, 4 from research institutes, and 11 (purchasing managers) from different
\par
retail enterprises were invited to fill the questionnaire for influence relationships of sustainable supplier
\par
evaluation criteria. The scale of pairwise comparison of the influence relationship using a score from
\par
0--4 is shown in Appendix A. We sent a paper questionnaire and electronic questionnaire to each
\par
expert; experts had the choice of returning it by e-mail or post. Each questionnaire took about 5--10
\par
min to compete. The data from the questionnaire were used in DEMATEL. In the second phase, after
\par
a month, we invited those 20 experts to help rate relative importance of the dimension and criteria
\par
in performance measure for sustainable supplier based on the pairwise comparison. The scale using
\par
scores from 0--9 is presented in Appendix B. Each questionnaire took about 10--15 min to compete.
\par
The data from the questionnaire were used in ANP. In the last phase, we invited 4 senior managers
\par
from the financial sector, the procurement sector, and the market sector in FX Supermarket to rate
\par
the social performance of four cuttlefish suppliers according to the history transaction record and
\par
market performance, as well as their experience and knowledge. The questionnaire for quantitative
\par
and qualitative criteria ratings is shown in Appendix C. Each questionnaire took about 10--20 min to
\par
compete. The data from the questionnaire were used in VIKOR. The entire process of data collection
\par
lasted three months, from May to July 2017.
\par
